1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,800
Project Checklists lives in the Proposal Engine
sidebar, under Build and estimate.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,991
It builds a checklist for one job from what that
job's scope actually says.

3
00:00:09,991 --> 00:00:14,811
Start from a proposal, upload a scope of work, or
paste one in.

4
00:00:14,811 --> 00:00:18,519
This walkthrough uses a training proposal, not a
client record.

5
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:20,002
Search for the proposal.

6
00:00:20,002 --> 00:00:24,822
Each result tells you what it holds, its displays
and its responsibility lines.

7
00:00:24,822 --> 00:00:27,047
Pick it and build the checklist.

8
00:00:28,147 --> 00:00:32,016
The engine reads the whole proposal: the displays,
the priced work under

9
00:00:32,016 --> 00:00:35,884
each one, the responsibility matrix, the scope of
work and the notes.

10
00:00:35,884 --> 00:00:40,398
Every item is written as an action, grouped into
phases from contract to closeout,

11
00:00:40,398 --> 00:00:42,977
and tagged with the display it belongs to.

12
00:00:42,977 --> 00:00:47,490
Open an item to see the exact sentence of the
proposal it came from.

13
00:00:47,490 --> 00:00:51,681
Where the responsibility matrix marks who does the
work, that is the owner.

14
00:00:51,681 --> 00:00:55,550
Filter by client to see everything the client owes
on this job.

15
00:00:56,650 --> 00:00:59,154
As the job moves, tick items off.

16
00:00:59,154 --> 00:01:02,374
The checklist records who ticked each one and when,

17
00:01:02,374 --> 00:01:04,878
and the progress on the left follows.

18
00:01:04,878 --> 00:01:09,529
Change an owner, or add a step the proposal did not
spell out.

19
00:01:09,529 --> 00:01:13,107
Everything saves as you go, for everyone working the
job.

20
00:01:14,207 --> 00:01:15,633
Take it with you.

21
00:01:15,633 --> 00:01:18,841
Excel gives your team a working sheet, with done

22
00:01:18,841 --> 00:01:21,337
and owner dropdowns and a live count.

23
00:01:21,337 --> 00:01:26,328
The PDF is the checklist phase by phase, with a box
beside every item.

24
00:01:27,428 --> 00:01:31,597
For a scope written for an installation
subcontractor, upload the document instead,

25
00:01:31,597 --> 00:01:34,376
say who it is written for, and build.

26
00:01:35,476 --> 00:01:39,253
When a scope repeats the same work for several
displays, each display

27
00:01:39,253 --> 00:01:40,512
gets its own items.

28
00:01:40,512 --> 00:01:43,344
Anything the scope excludes is listed as by others,

29
00:01:43,344 --> 00:01:45,862
so you can confirm who is covering it.

30
00:01:45,862 --> 00:01:48,694
One checklist per job, built from its own scope.
